P2 features complete — 2026-07-29

## Feature 1: Employee Management
Backend:
- apps/api/src/employees/dto/employee.dto.ts (CreateEmployeeDto, UpdateEmployeeDto)
- apps/api/src/employees/employees.service.ts (list, findOne, create w/ bcrypt, update, deactivate)
- apps/api/src/employees/employees.controller.ts (GET /employees, GET /employees/:id, POST, PATCH, DELETE)
- apps/api/src/employees/employees.module.ts
- Registered EmployeesModule in app.module.ts
- Auth: JwtAuthGuard + RolesGuard (RESTAURANT_OWNER | BRANCH_MANAGER only)

Frontend:
- apps/admin/src/app/(dashboard)/employees/page.tsx
  - Staff table: Name, Email, Role badge (color-coded), Branch, Status, Actions
  - Add Staff modal (name, email, password, role select, branch select)
  - Edit Staff modal (name, role, branch — no password)
  - Deactivate/reactivate toggle (DELETE → soft delete, PATCH isActive=true → reactivate)
- Added "Staff" nav item (UserCog icon) to sidebar between Customers and Tables

## Feature 2: Delivery Ordering Support
Backend:
- Added deliveryAddress String? to Order model in schema.prisma
- Migration: 20260728205258_add_delivery_address applied
- Added deliveryAddress?: string field to CreateOrderDto
- orders.service.ts createOrder: throws BadRequestException if DELIVERY and no deliveryAddress
- deliveryAddress persisted to Order record on create

Frontend (customer-web):
- menu/[restaurantId]/page.tsx: added orderType state ("DINE_IN" | "DELIVERY")
- Cart drawer: two-button selector (🪑 Dine In / 🚚 Delivery) at top
- Dine-In: shows table info from URL
- Delivery: shows textarea for delivery address (validated before submit)
- submitOrder passes orderType + deliveryAddress in POST /orders/public payload

## Feature 3: Analytics Reports
Backend:
- analytics.service.ts: added getReport() dispatcher + 6 private methods:
  getTodaySales, getDaywiseSales, getItemWiseSales (groupBy workaround for Prisma circular-type),
  getPaymentModeBreakdown, getCancelledOrders, getTopCustomers
- analytics.controller.ts: GET /analytics/reports/:type?from=&to=&branchId=

Frontend:
- analytics/page.tsx: Reports section below existing charts
  - 6 report type tabs: Today Sales | Day-wise | Item-wise | Payment Modes | Cancelled | Top Customers
  - Date range pickers (from/to), default last 7 days
  - "Run Report" button with spinner
  - ReportTable component renders appropriate columns per report type

